<title>USA: Armstrong buys control of Skanska unit.</title>
<headline>Armstrong buys control of Skanska unit.</headline>
<dateline>LANCASTER, Pa. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Armstrong World Industries said on Monday it acquired 51 percent of the Swedish flooring manufacturer Holmsund Golv AB from Skanska AB for an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Along with Holmsund, Armstrong also acquired its distributor subsidiary Nya Leksells AB. The deal is part of Armstrong's continuing strategy to expand its European operations, the company said.</p>
<p>Armstrong makes interior furnishings, including floor coverings. The company also makes gasketing materials for the automotive market.</p>
